Now, you might be wondering, "What are endocrine disruptors?" Well, imagine there are tiny soldiers inside our bodies called hormones. Hormones help our body grow, give us energy, and control how we feel. Endocrine disruptors are chemicals that might confuse those soldiers, causing them not to work properly. They can be found in some of our everyday items like plastic bottles or cans.

The European Court of Justice says that the people in charge should be catching these harmful chemicals more quickly and making them against the rules. They think that by acting fast, they can make sure that all of us – kids, grown-ups, and animals too – will be safer and healthier.

In short, the court's decision is a reminder that it's important to keep an eye out for anything that might cause harm, so that it doesn't get a chance to hurt us. Just like our parents and teachers watch out for us on the playground, the European Commission should be watching out and protecting everyone from these sneaky chemicals called endocrine disruptors.
